ng data contamination in large language models.\n718\t\\newblock In \\emph{ICLR}, 2024.\n719\t\n720\t\\bibitem[Guo et al.(2017)]{guo2017calibration}\n721\tC.~Guo, G.~Pleiss, Y.~Sun, and K.~Q. Weinberger.\n722\t\\newblock On calibration of modern neural networks.\n723\t\\newblock In \\emph{ICML}, 2017.\n724\t\n725\t\\bibitem[Holland and Wainer(1993)]{holland1993dif}\n726\tP.~W. Holland and H.~Wainer.\n727\t\\newblock \\emph{Differential Item Functioning}.\n728\t\\newblock Erlbaum, 1993.\n729\t\n730\t\\bibitem[Lalor et al.(2024)]{lalor2024aaai}\n731\tJ.~P. Lalor, P.~Rodriguez, and J.~Hernandez-Orallo.\n732\t\\newblock Benchmarking large language models using item response theory.\n733\t\\newblock In \\emph{AAAI}, 2024.\n734\t\n735\t\\bibitem[Liang et al.(2023)]{liang2023helm}\n736\tP.~Liang et al.\n737\t\\newblock Holistic evaluation of language models.\n738\t\\newblock \\emph{Transactions on Machine Learning Research}, 2023.\n739\t\n740\t\\bibitem[LiveBench(2024)]{livebench2024}\n741\tC.~White et al.\n742\t\\newblock LiveBench: A challenging, contamination-free LLM benchmark.\n743\t\\newblock \\emph{arXiv preprint arXiv:2406.19314}, 2024.\n744\t\n745\t\\bibitem[Mislevy(1986)]{mislevy1986}\n746\tR.~J. Mislevy.\n747\t\\newblock Recent developments in the factor analysis of categorical variables.\n748\t\\newblock \\emph{Journal of Educational Statistics}, 11(1):3--31, 1986.\n749\t\n750\t\\bibitem[Oren et al.(2024)]{oren2024dcr}\n751\tY.~Oren et al.\n752\t\\newblock Proving test set contamination in black box language models.\n753\t\\newblock In \\emph{EMNLP}, 2024.\n754\t\n755\t\\bibitem[Park et al.(2023)]{park2023trak}\n756\tS.~M. Park, K.~Georgiev, A.~Ilyas, G.~Leclerc, and A.~Madry.\n757\t\\newblock TRAK: Attributing model behavior at scale.\n758\t\\newblock In \\emph{ICML}, 2023.\n759\t\n760\t\\bibitem[Platt(1999)]{platt1999probabilistic}\n761\tJ.~Platt.\n762\t\\newblock Probabilistic outputs for support vector machines.\n763\t\\newblock In \\emph{Advances in Large Margin Classifiers}, 1999.\n764\t\n765\t\\bibitem[Polo et al.(2024)]{polo2024tinybenchmarks}\n766\tF.~M. Polo et al.\n767\t\\newblock TinyBenchmarks: evaluating LLMs with fewer examples.\n768\t\\newblock In \\emph{ICML}, 2024.\n769\t\n770\t\\bibitem[Pruthi et al.(2020)]{pruthi2020tracin}\n771\tG.~Pruthi, F.~Liu, S.~Kale, and M.~Sundararajan.\n772\t\\newblock Estimating training data influence by tracing gradient descent.\n773\t\\newblock In \\emph{NeurIPS}, 2020.\n774\t\n775\t\\bibitem[Raju et al.(2024)]{raju2024growingpains}\n776\tK.~Raju et al.\n777\t\\newblock Growing pains: Understanding evaluation dynamics of LLMs with IRT.\n778\t\\newblock \\emph{arXiv preprint}, 2024.\n779\t\n780\t\\bibitem[Reckase(2009)]{reckase2009multidimensional}\n781\tM.~D. Reckase.\n782\t\\newblock \\emph{Multidimensional Item Response Theory}.\n783\t\\newblock Springer, 2009.\n784\t\n785\t\\bibitem[Shi et al.(2024)]{shi2024cdd}\n786\tW.~Shi et al.\n787\t\\newblock Detecting pretraining data from large language models.\n788\t\\newblock In \\emph{ICLR}, 2024.\n789\t\n790\t\\bibitem[Shokri et al.(2017)]{shokri2017membership}\n791\tR.~Shokri, M.~Stronati, C.~Song, and V.~Shmatikov.\n792\t\\newblock Membership inference attacks against machine learning models.\n793\t\\newblock In \\emph{IEEE S\\&P}, 2017.\n794\t\n795\t\\bibitem[Sinharay(2017)]{sinharay2017assessment}\n796\tS.~Sinharay.\n797\t\\newblock Detection of item preknowledge using likelihood ratio test and score test.\n798\t\\newblock \\emph{Journal of Educational and Behavioral Statistics}, 42(1):46--68, 2017.\n799\t\n800\t\\bibitem[Talts et al.(2018)]{talts2018sbc}\n801\tS.~Talts, M.~Betancourt, D.~Simpson, A.~Vehtari, and A.~Gelman.\n802\t\\newblock Validating Bayesian inference algorithms with simulation-based calibration.\n803\t\\newblock \\emph{arXiv preprint arXiv:1804.06788}, 2018.\n804\t\n805\t\\bibitem[Thissen et al.(1993)]{thissen1993dif}\n806\tD.~Thissen, L.~Steinberg, and H.~Wainer.\n807\t\\newblock Detection of differential item functioning using the parameters of item response models.\n808\t\\newblock In \\emph{Differential Item Functioning}, pages 67--113. Erlbaum, 1993.\n809\t\n810\t\\bibitem[Weller et al.(2024)]{weller2024selfcritique}\n811\tO.~Weller et al.\n812\t\\newblock Self-contamination: Can LLMs detect their own training data?\n813\t\\newblock \\emph{arXiv preprint}, 2024.\n814\t\n815\t\\bibitem[Yang et al.(2023)]{yang2023rethinking}\n816\tS.~Yang et al.\n817\t\\newblock Rethinking benchmark and contamination for language models with rephrased samples.\n818\t\\newblock \\emph{arXiv preprint arXiv:2311.04850}, 2023.\n819\t\n820\t\\bibitem[Zhang et al.(2024)]{zhang2024minkpp}\n821\tY.~Zhang et al.\n822\t\\newblock Min-K\\%++: Improved baseline for detecting pre-training data from large language models.\n823\t\\newblock In \\emph{ICML}, 2024.\n824\t\n825\t\\bibitem[Zheng et al.(2023)]{zheng2023chatbot}\n826\tL.~Zheng et al.\n827\t\\newblock Judging LLM-as-a-judge with MT-Bench and Chatbot Arena.\n828\t\\newblock In \\emph{NeurIPS}, 2023.\n829\t\n830\t\\bibitem[Zumbo(1999)]{zumbo1999dif}\n831\tB.~D. Zumbo.\n832\t\\newblock A handbook on the theory and methods of differential item functioning (DIF).\n833\t\\newblock Technical report, National Defense Headquarters, Ottawa, 1999.\n834\t\n835\t\\end{thebibliography}\n836\t\n837\t\\end{document}\n838\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01UVPJeteNu9kkU463iUdhXw","session_id":"2e2bc174-5249-4ea4-a7dc-2e60f9f53d62","uuid":"bc381b88-04ff-4d66-aaa5-bb585d7db450","timestamp":"2026-05-15T06:30:48.241Z"}
